Let's implement generating user profile improvement. Current solution only supports manul creation of User Profile Memory (UPN). I want to improve that by implementing continues UPN update. This new approach will:
- let the LLM model decide whether to update / create UPN
- remove the risk of LLM missconfigure the actual JSON structure of UPN
- streamlines the UPM maintanace

What needs to be done:
- extend the master prompt template with instructions to consider current user request / message and decide whether it contains any notable user interestes, preferences, etc. and if so, proceed with update
- create a new tool called "update_user_profile" which will be triggered by the preceeding bullet
- the LLM Model (master prompt) is calling the tool with Use of  RFC 7396 (JSON Merge Patch–style semantics) which generates
- the tool will implemnt the Use RFC 7396 (JSON Merge Patch–style semantics) to our CosmosDB which stores the UPN

The initial UPN's JSON structure is:

{
  "profile_changed": true or false,
  "change_summary": "Brief description of what changed, or 'No new personal information found'",
  "facts_added": 0,
  "facts_updated": 0,
  "facts_removed": 0,
  "profile": {
    "basic_info": { ... },
    "interests": [ ... ],
    "habits": [ ... ],
    "preferences": { ... },
    "status": { ... },
    "facts": [ ... ]
  }
}

Create a carefull design for this feature only, no code yet.
